00:17:16.369 --> 00:17:20.900
Not really.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:22.900
Teen mysteriously saved in Lake.

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:25.900
Girl rescued in robbery.

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:26.900
Freak accident saves woman.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:30.900
Now, all those happened right around the time that you and Chloe were in the ninth grade.

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.900
Would Chloe give you all this?

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:37.900
Because I take pictures for a living doesn't mean I don't know my way around a search engine.

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:39.900
Whatever.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:40.900
I think that there's a...

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:44.900
real possibility that you went to school with this guy.

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:46.900
And what makes you say that?

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:48.900
Look at all the people involved who went to Smallville High.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:52.900
Then right around the time that you guys graduated, these mysterious incidents,

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:58.339
they started popping up more often in Metropolis.

00:17:58.339 --> 00:18:02.859
What's your point?

00:18:02.859 --> 00:18:06.859
Yeah, I'm just wondering if anyone at Smallville High stood out.

00:18:06.859 --> 00:18:13.029
You know, I had hero potential.

00:18:13.029 --> 00:18:19.380
No, not that I can think of.

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:25.170
But even if this guy did exist, don't you think it's his decision to go public?

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:26.170
go public?

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:27.170
I don't know.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:29.170
I mean, maybe a little gentle prodding.

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:31.170
I mean, I might be doing some good.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:34.960
I mean, it's not really your choice to make.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:43.319
Be careful with that, Jimmy.

00:18:43.319 --> 00:18:44.319
It's fragile.

00:18:44.319 --> 00:18:49.559
Since when you take such an interest in my family's photographs?

00:18:49.559 --> 00:19:08.230
What is it?

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:10.230
Look, Jimmy, I got a lot of work to do.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:13.230
I gotta fix a tractor, so...

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:15.230
It's all so clear.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:19.220
That's what's been going on between you and Chloe.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.220
She's known this whole time, and...

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:25.720
Now this picture.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:26.720
Jimmy.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:30.900
You're not making any sense.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:31.900
Oh, it makes perfect sense.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:35.299
It's you.

00:19:35.299 --> 00:19:58.420
Isn't it?

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:03.930
Over love.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:04.930
Chloe?

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:05.930
Jimmy knows my secret.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:06.930
What?

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.930
Between the research and these family photos, he put it together.

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:11.930
Oh my God. What did you do?

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:13.930
I denied it. I didn't know what else to do.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:15.930
I told him I had chores and then I came over here.

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:16.930
Chloe, this is not good.

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:18.930
I'm so sorry, clerk. I should have listened to you.

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:21.930
I had no idea he could pick you out of a lineup.

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:23.930
Not from that blurry mugshot.

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:25.930
The important thing is that we find a way to throw him off the trail,

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:26.930
for his own good.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:31.809
You beat me here.

00:20:31.809 --> 00:20:33.809
Jimmy!

00:20:33.809 --> 00:20:36.809
When I left you, you were doing chores.

00:20:36.809 --> 00:20:37.809
You blurred over here, didn't you?

00:20:37.809 --> 00:20:39.809
Jimmy, that's ridiculous.

00:20:39.809 --> 00:20:41.809
I used all the shortcuts.

00:20:41.809 --> 00:20:45.809
What? What shortcut? I was speeding the whole way.

00:20:45.809 --> 00:20:48.809
Oh, you know what, Clark? Why don't you show me on a map?

00:20:48.809 --> 00:20:49.809
Jimmy.

00:20:49.809 --> 00:20:51.809
This isn't a witch hunt.

00:20:51.809 --> 00:20:53.809
You've known this whole time.

00:20:53.809 --> 00:20:56.809
That's the big secret that you've been keeping from me.

00:20:56.809 --> 00:20:58.809
And I get it.

00:20:58.809 --> 00:20:59.809
I get it.

00:20:59.809 --> 00:21:01.809
And of course you want to keep it a secret,

00:21:01.809 --> 00:21:03.809
but you can trust me, CK. I got your back.

00:21:03.809 --> 00:21:05.809
And I appreciate that, Jimmy.

00:21:05.809 --> 00:21:07.809
But this deep dark secret that you believe in

00:21:07.809 --> 00:21:09.809
so strongly just doesn't exist.

00:21:09.809 --> 00:21:11.809
Like, I'm sorry to let you down.

00:21:11.809 --> 00:21:14.809
Chloe, you think you'll tell me the truth, right?

00:21:14.809 --> 00:21:16.809
Yeah, I mean, the truth is, as much as I wish

00:21:16.809 --> 00:21:19.809
that Clark could shatter Land's Speed records.

00:21:19.809 --> 00:21:20.809
It's just...

00:21:20.809 --> 00:21:25.339
He's just a regular guy.

00:21:25.339 --> 00:21:27.339
You don't trust me, do you?

00:21:27.339 --> 00:21:29.339
She's right, Jimmy.

00:21:29.339 --> 00:21:31.339
There's nothing special about me whatsoever.

00:21:31.339 --> 00:21:36.150
Then I guess I'll have to prove it.

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:43.259
Jimmy.

00:21:43.259 --> 00:22:10.069
Hey, man, uh, listen, if you're looking for a little jaunt to Aruba,

00:22:10.069 --> 00:22:12.069
you're gonna have to find another plane, because this one's packed.

00:22:12.069 --> 00:22:15.069
It's all full, and, uh, we're about ready for takeoff.

00:22:15.069 --> 00:22:16.069
No way.

00:22:16.069 --> 00:22:20.069
When your assistant said you were having your pre-flight drinks, she wasn't kidding.

00:22:20.069 --> 00:22:21.069
No, she was not.

00:22:21.069 --> 00:22:23.069
I hope the pilot's at least sober.

00:22:23.069 --> 00:22:25.069
Well, I sure hope the pilot's sober, too, Clark.

00:22:25.069 --> 00:22:26.069
He's got to get us there.

00:22:26.069 --> 00:22:29.069
You know what it is, though, honestly, you just got to get in the right frame of mind

00:22:29.069 --> 00:22:30.069
if you're gonna fly the friendly skies.

00:22:30.069 --> 00:22:31.069
Not right, ladies.

00:22:31.069 --> 00:22:32.069
Yeah.

00:22:32.069 --> 00:22:33.069
Uh.

00:22:34.069 --> 00:22:35.069
I need to talk to you.

00:22:35.069 --> 00:22:36.069
You know what, Clark?

00:22:36.069 --> 00:22:39.069
Actually, right now, not the greatest time for me.

00:22:39.069 --> 00:22:40.069
But I tell you what I can do.

00:22:40.069 --> 00:22:42.069
I drop you a postcard, okay?

00:22:42.069 --> 00:22:44.069
It's urgent.

00:22:44.069 --> 00:22:48.319
Uh, uh, thank you, please.

00:22:48.319 --> 00:23:00.380
Let's go grab a drink.

00:23:00.380 --> 00:23:03.380
Look what you did.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:06.380
So, what's the latest crisis in your life, Clark?

00:23:06.380 --> 00:23:08.380
Did you just come here to lecture me about drinking and flying?

00:23:08.380 --> 00:23:10.380
Jimmy's on to my secret.

00:23:10.380 --> 00:23:11.380
He's got this picture.

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:13.380
And you're afraid that he's gonna plaster it all over the front page of the planet.

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:14.380
the front page of the planet.

00:23:14.380 --> 00:23:15.380
Is that it?

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:16.380
Yeah.

00:23:16.380 --> 00:23:18.380
You know, that might not be such a bad idea.

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:21.380
Sure would force you to step up a little bit.

00:23:21.380 --> 00:23:24.690
What happened to you?

00:23:24.690 --> 00:23:26.690
You've all been given up on the Green Arrow.

00:23:26.690 --> 00:23:30.690
Did you know that Lois was mung to block him away from your apartment?

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:33.690
It seems that every time someone sees you, you have a drink in your hand.

00:23:33.690 --> 00:23:35.690
Maybe I'm not the one who needs to step up.

00:23:35.690 --> 00:23:43.710
You just need to relax, okay?

00:23:43.710 --> 00:23:46.710
Sometimes even superheroes need to take a vacation.

00:23:46.710 --> 00:23:48.710
Oliver, I understand that you're still upset with me.

00:23:48.710 --> 00:23:49.710
I knew that line.

00:23:49.710 --> 00:23:51.710
killed your parents and I didn't tell you.

00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:52.710
I made a decision.

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:54.710
And maybe it was the wrong one,

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:59.140
but you're the only one who can help me right now.

00:23:59.140 --> 00:24:00.140
I'll tell you what.

00:24:00.140 --> 00:24:02.140
Clark, I'll call you when I get back.

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:04.140
There's no time, Oliver.

00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:06.140
People have died because they know my secrets.

00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:08.140
Lives have been turned upside down.

00:24:08.140 --> 00:24:12.140
I can't mind wipe the people who already know my secret.

00:24:12.140 --> 00:24:15.140
I can only do my best to protect the people like Jimmy.

00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:23.500
Do it for me.

00:24:23.500 --> 00:24:24.500
Do it for him.

00:24:24.500 --> 00:24:36.180
He's an innocent bystander whose life will never be the same.

00:24:36.180 --> 00:24:37.180
So there's bombs going off everywhere.

00:24:37.180 --> 00:24:38.180
There's bombs going off everywhere.

00:24:38.180 --> 00:24:39.880
next to me gets shot.

00:24:39.880 --> 00:24:42.180
So the lieutenant turns to me, grabs my notebook,

00:24:42.180 --> 00:24:45.180
first bees it out the Humvee window, and sticks an M16 on my hand.

00:24:45.180 --> 00:24:46.680
Wait a minute.

00:24:46.680 --> 00:24:49.680
I thought you said your notebook made it all the way to Baghdadden back.

00:24:49.680 --> 00:24:50.680
It did.

00:24:50.680 --> 00:24:53.680
Once the smoke cleared, I walked about a mile and a half to go find it.

00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:55.680
Wow.

00:24:55.680 --> 00:24:57.680
So what about the last few years?

00:24:57.680 --> 00:25:00.680
What kind of misadventures have you had?

00:25:00.680 --> 00:25:03.680
Come on, you can be honest about your past?

00:25:03.680 --> 00:25:05.680
Where do I start?

00:25:05.680 --> 00:25:07.680
Any big investigations?

00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:09.680
You know, where you went deep undercover,

00:25:09.680 --> 00:25:12.680
with the drug lord or crime family

00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:15.680
or maximum security prison?

00:25:15.680 --> 00:25:17.680
Okay, bullets flying over my head is one thing,

00:25:17.680 --> 00:25:20.680
but stick me in a tiny little cell, no thank you.

00:25:20.680 --> 00:25:23.680
Cosperphobia's a bitch.

00:25:23.680 --> 00:25:27.680
So you've never, you know, seen the inside of a big government facility?

00:25:27.680 --> 00:25:30.680
Because that would be a great expose waiting to happen.

00:25:30.680 --> 00:25:36.039
You want to hear about the last time I was in a big government facility?

00:25:36.039 --> 00:25:41.529
I think I was in high school.

00:25:41.529 --> 00:25:43.529
It's about as close to prison as it is against.

00:25:43.529 --> 00:25:44.529
Really?

00:25:44.529 --> 00:25:50.529
Have you ever had your palms red?

00:25:50.529 --> 00:25:55.220
I don't do too well with fortune tellers.

00:25:55.220 --> 00:25:59.220
The last one I went to see told me that I was destined to fall for a guy who

00:25:59.220 --> 00:26:02.220
flies a lot and likes to wear tights.

00:26:02.220 --> 00:26:06.220
So I'm just waiting for my cross-dressing pilot to make his landing.

00:26:06.220 --> 00:26:09.789
Well, I'll tell you the good stuff, then.

00:26:09.789 --> 00:26:17.089
Give me our hand.

00:26:17.089 --> 00:26:24.269
Okay.

00:26:24.269 --> 00:26:29.049
I made it all the way to bag down there.

00:26:29.049 --> 00:26:36.450
Wilson.

00:26:36.450 --> 00:26:38.450
The abilities are classified.

00:26:38.450 --> 00:26:40.450
How is he said?

00:26:40.450 --> 00:26:41.450
I knew it.

00:26:41.450 --> 00:26:42.450
You were in black crew.

00:26:42.450 --> 00:26:50.210
Black Creek.

00:26:50.210 --> 00:26:53.880
So, am I going to live?

00:26:53.880 --> 00:27:00.069
Excuse me.

00:27:00.069 --> 00:27:02.069
I should take this. I'll be back in a moment.

00:27:02.069 --> 00:27:03.069
Okay.

00:27:03.069 --> 00:27:23.019
So are you and Lois getting to know each other?

00:27:23.019 --> 00:27:27.019
I scanned her. She doesn't have your artifact. I know that much.

00:27:27.019 --> 00:27:31.359
Anything besides air and that brain of hers?

00:27:31.359 --> 00:27:33.359
She's figured out who I am.

00:27:33.359 --> 00:27:39.940
She has this flash drive from Black Creek.

00:27:39.940 --> 00:27:45.920
But when she stole from the library, the facility's been dismantled.

00:27:45.920 --> 00:27:47.920
There's nothing on that that could implicate Luther Court?

00:27:47.920 --> 00:27:49.920
It implicates me.

00:27:49.920 --> 00:27:50.920
She knows the truth.

00:27:50.920 --> 00:27:51.920
about what I can do.

00:27:51.920 --> 00:27:59.180
Well, it sounds like you're in a bit of a quagmire,

00:27:59.180 --> 00:28:02.180
especially in light of the fact that she's an overzealous newspaper reporter.

00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:09.660
I want to find yourself in a reporter.

00:28:09.660 --> 00:28:12.660
Something tells me Lois Lane won't be coming in to work tomorrow.

00:28:12.660 --> 00:28:21.420
Move on to our next person of interest.

00:28:21.420 --> 00:28:40.319
Jimmy Olson.

00:28:40.319 --> 00:28:42.319
Well, then, thanks for dinner.

00:28:42.319 --> 00:28:45.319
Now you'll be able to make it across town without a tour book in your hand.

00:28:45.319 --> 00:28:47.319
Hey, you said you had that extra transit map.

00:28:47.319 --> 00:28:51.660
When I come up and get it, we can have a nightcap.

00:28:51.660 --> 00:28:52.660
I like nightcap.

00:28:52.660 --> 00:28:55.660
but unfortunately I'm on a lethal deadline.

00:28:55.660 --> 00:28:58.660
I have to prove you to 5,000 word or do at dawn.

00:28:58.660 --> 00:29:00.660
I'm a hell of a speller.

00:29:00.660 --> 00:29:02.660
Wouldn't I come up and give you a hand?

00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:05.660
Thanks, but spell check is actually my best friend.

00:29:05.660 --> 00:29:07.660
See you, maniana.

00:29:07.660 --> 00:29:27.960
No one can know who I am.

00:29:27.960 --> 00:29:29.960
I need that flash drive.

00:29:29.960 --> 00:29:46.009
Are you ready?

00:29:46.009 --> 00:29:47.009
Ready as I'll ever be.

00:29:47.009 --> 00:29:51.009
I don't enjoy driving a speeding car at anyone, even you.

00:29:51.009 --> 00:29:53.009
It's okay, Chloe.

00:29:53.009 --> 00:29:54.009
Someone's gonna save me.

00:29:54.009 --> 00:29:57.450
That's him now.

00:29:57.450 --> 00:30:02.369
I'll remember 10 o'clock on the dot.

00:30:02.369 --> 00:30:04.369
Tell me you're sober.

00:30:04.369 --> 00:30:05.369
Let me tell you something.

00:30:05.369 --> 00:30:06.369
I wish I wasn't sober.

00:30:06.369 --> 00:30:08.369
I could be in a cabana and a ruba right now.

00:30:08.369 --> 00:30:11.369
Instead, I'm hanging out in the middle of downtown on a rooftop with you guys.

00:30:11.369 --> 00:30:13.369
You didn't hear me complain when I had to put on green leather

00:30:13.369 --> 00:30:15.369
to protect your identity.

00:30:15.369 --> 00:30:17.369
Clark, you made out with my girlfriend, man.

00:30:17.369 --> 00:30:18.369
What'd you have to complain about?

00:30:18.369 --> 00:30:23.700
Jimmy's gonna be here any second.

00:30:23.700 --> 00:30:26.700
We cross at 10 and Oliver.

00:30:26.700 --> 00:30:28.700
Don't screw this up.

00:30:28.700 --> 00:30:30.700
Just keep your fingers,

00:30:30.700 --> 00:30:33.329
Ross.

00:30:33.329 --> 00:30:35.329
Jimmy, thanks for meeting me.

00:30:35.329 --> 00:30:38.329
Clerk, I want you to know that no matter what you tell me,

00:30:38.329 --> 00:30:40.329
I'm not going to look at you any differently.

00:30:40.329 --> 00:30:42.329
That would be the same LCCA to me.

00:30:42.329 --> 00:30:48.750
I swear, ask anyone.

00:30:48.750 --> 00:30:52.220
I know how to keep a secret.

00:30:52.220 --> 00:30:56.950
You recognize me at the daily planet.

00:30:56.950 --> 00:30:58.950
And I can just as easily forget.

00:30:58.950 --> 00:31:00.950
I have a terrible memory.

00:31:00.950 --> 00:31:10.309
There's one thing you learn.

00:31:10.309 --> 00:31:17.579
When you get locked up in a cage for four years, many as you don't.

00:31:17.579 --> 00:31:28.880
Jimmy, let's go get some car.

00:31:28.880 --> 00:31:30.880
Let's go get some coffee.

00:31:30.880 --> 00:31:32.880
Set the record straight once and for all.

00:31:32.880 --> 00:31:34.880
Whatever you comfortable, man, I'm here for you.

00:31:34.880 --> 00:31:41.230
I'm sorry, Lois, but I'm never going to be locked up again.

00:31:41.230 --> 00:32:10.680
On the move, Oliver.

00:32:10.680 --> 00:32:19.470
Let's just get this over with, huh?

00:32:19.470 --> 00:32:48.849
Hello?

00:32:48.849 --> 00:32:50.849
Listen, I'm, I need to make a phone call. Just wait right here.

00:32:50.849 --> 00:32:52.849
Now? Yeah, I'll be right back.

00:32:52.849 --> 00:33:25.819
Going with me.

00:33:25.819 --> 00:33:26.819
What?

00:33:26.819 --> 00:33:28.819
Oh, hey man. Just take my wallet.

00:33:28.819 --> 00:33:29.819
I don't want your money.

00:33:29.819 --> 00:33:38.539
This isn't part of the plan.

00:33:38.539 --> 00:34:11.099
Jimmy. What happened?

00:34:11.099 --> 00:34:15.099
Do you actually expect me to fall for that?

00:34:15.099 --> 00:34:18.099
I know exactly what happened. You just saved me.

00:34:18.099 --> 00:34:21.099
Jimmy, I wish I could take the credit, but it wasn't me.

00:34:21.099 --> 00:34:23.099
He's him.

00:34:23.099 --> 00:35:20.489
I'm so sorry, CK.

00:35:20.489 --> 00:35:21.489
Congratulations, Jimmy.

00:35:21.489 --> 00:35:23.489
I think that I just about pulled you out of a closet.

00:35:23.489 --> 00:35:25.489
You weren't even in. I felt terrible.

00:35:25.489 --> 00:35:27.489
I don't feel too bad.

00:35:27.489 --> 00:35:30.489
Actually, I'm honored you thought I could move with lightning speed.

00:35:30.489 --> 00:35:35.489
Well, you might not be superhuman, Clark, but there's a reason that I thought you were to get some air.

00:35:35.489 --> 00:35:36.489
Why is that?

00:35:36.489 --> 00:35:38.489
Girl Scout cookies twice a year?

00:35:38.489 --> 00:35:39.489
Seriously.

00:35:39.489 --> 00:35:41.489
You're the kind of guy that people can count on,

00:35:41.489 --> 00:35:43.489
whether it's your friends or strangers.

00:35:43.489 --> 00:35:44.489
No, he's there for them.

00:35:44.489 --> 00:35:46.739
That's rare.

00:35:46.739 --> 00:35:56.079
What's rare? A pen that works in this place?

00:35:56.079 --> 00:35:58.079
I heard about your date last night.

00:35:58.079 --> 00:35:59.079
Ended with a thud.

00:35:59.079 --> 00:36:04.250
Sorry I didn't get your phone call till it was all over.

00:36:04.250 --> 00:36:05.250
I wasn't on a date. Smallville.

00:36:05.250 --> 00:36:08.250
I was deep undercover on a dinner with a psychopath.

00:36:08.250 --> 00:36:10.250
Sounds like your type.

00:36:10.250 --> 00:36:13.250
Lois, why didn't you tell me you're working on a story?

00:36:13.250 --> 00:36:16.250
If I told you my secret, it would have put you in harm,

00:36:16.250 --> 00:36:19.820
It was for your own safety.

00:36:19.820 --> 00:36:20.820
Thanks for looking out for me.

00:36:20.820 --> 00:36:22.820
You're welcome.

00:36:22.820 --> 00:36:26.820
Hey, Lois, have any chance you take a peek at today's front page?

00:36:26.820 --> 00:36:30.070
I certainly did, Jimmy Olson.

00:36:30.070 --> 00:36:33.070
I have to say that I've underestimated you.

00:36:33.070 --> 00:36:37.070
As hard as it is to believe, I was saved now twice.

00:36:37.070 --> 00:36:39.070
In two days.

00:36:39.070 --> 00:36:44.070
Without a doubt, I'm officially a true believer in this red and blue super dude.

00:36:44.070 --> 00:36:46.070
Hey, Jimmy. Hey.

00:36:46.070 --> 00:36:47.070
Oh, hey, guys.

00:36:47.070 --> 00:36:48.070
Good job.

00:36:48.070 --> 00:36:51.880
Word from above.

00:36:51.880 --> 00:36:54.880
The mayor is going to announce the new fire chief at 10 a.m.

00:36:54.880 --> 00:36:58.880
My days of covering Yonner press conferences are all but over.

00:36:58.880 --> 00:37:01.880
Because I have a new mission in life.

00:37:01.880 --> 00:37:03.880
I didn't realize you had an old one.

00:37:03.880 --> 00:37:09.260
I'm going to use my expert tracking skills and find this camera-shy superhero.

00:37:09.260 --> 00:37:13.260
Really? Good luck with that.

00:37:13.260 --> 00:37:15.260
Mark my words, Clark Kent.

00:37:15.260 --> 00:37:21.260
I won't stop until I land the first worldwide exclusive interview.

00:37:21.260 --> 00:37:25.139
Watch me.

00:37:25.139 --> 00:37:36.570
Nice press.

00:37:36.570 --> 00:37:40.570
I got to tell you, I never realized how photogenic you were,

00:37:40.570 --> 00:37:42.570
as long as no one sees your face.

00:37:42.570 --> 00:37:44.570
Could have been a lot worse.

00:37:44.570 --> 00:37:47.570
Yeah, it could have.

00:37:47.570 --> 00:37:49.570
I'm surprised you let the thing print, though.

00:37:49.570 --> 00:37:52.570
I was expecting to hear about some last-minute computer meltdown at the planet.

00:37:52.570 --> 00:37:56.039
To be honest, it did cross my mind.

00:37:56.039 --> 00:37:59.039
But then I got to thinking.

00:37:59.039 --> 00:38:03.610
Maybe my destiny is more than just secretly saving people.

00:38:03.610 --> 00:38:08.780
Maybe it was also to give people hope.

00:38:08.780 --> 00:38:10.780
Someone to believe in.

00:38:10.780 --> 00:38:14.570
I knew you to catch you to catch on someday.

00:38:14.570 --> 00:38:21.239
Well, I just want to say thank you before you want on vacation.

00:38:21.239 --> 00:38:23.239
Vacation's over, Clark.

00:38:23.239 --> 00:38:25.239
I'm headed to Europe.

00:38:25.239 --> 00:38:26.239
On business?

00:38:26.239 --> 00:38:28.239
Uh, yeah, kinda. Kinda.

00:38:28.239 --> 00:38:29.239
You know my friends?

00:38:29.239 --> 00:38:31.239
I just like to dress up and kick ass.

00:38:31.239 --> 00:38:33.239
We're having a summit.

00:38:33.239 --> 00:38:35.239
What happened to the party plane?

00:38:35.239 --> 00:38:39.119
Wouldn't know the truth?

00:38:39.119 --> 00:38:40.119
I don't know.

00:38:40.119 --> 00:38:43.119
When I was zipping across the street taking that punk down,

00:38:43.119 --> 00:38:47.119
I finally felt like myself again, you know?

00:38:47.119 --> 00:38:48.119
You know?

00:38:48.119 --> 00:38:50.119
Because that's who I am.

00:38:50.119 --> 00:38:54.119
I'm not the party boy who runs off on these lost, rum-soaked weekends.

00:38:54.119 --> 00:38:56.119
I'm not the multinational corporate titan.

00:38:56.119 --> 00:38:57.119
That's not me.

00:38:57.119 --> 00:39:03.909
Underneath it all, the person I really am is Green Arrow.

00:39:03.909 --> 00:39:13.719
Glad you finally come around.

00:39:13.719 --> 00:39:17.719
Clark, I understand why you didn't tell me about my parents' murder.

00:39:17.719 --> 00:39:21.920
You were afraid of how I'd take it.

00:39:21.920 --> 00:39:22.920
And I...

00:39:22.920 --> 00:39:25.920
It's fine. You were right.

00:39:25.920 --> 00:39:30.400
Once I found out, I'm pretty sure my parents wouldn't have been proud of how I reacted.

00:39:30.400 --> 00:39:31.400
proud of how I reacted.

00:39:31.400 --> 00:39:38.849
Oliver, I have no doubt that your parents would be proud of the person you've become.

00:39:38.849 --> 00:39:44.800
Except for one thing, and it's just a piece of friendly advice.

00:39:44.800 --> 00:39:48.909
Don't ever wear that cape again.

00:39:48.909 --> 00:39:50.909
It looked ridiculous.

00:39:50.909 --> 00:39:53.909
Really? I kind of liked it.

00:39:53.909 --> 00:39:55.909
Sure help with the aerodynamics.

00:39:55.909 --> 00:39:58.909
You should give it a try.

00:39:58.909 --> 00:40:01.380
Not in this lifetime.

00:40:01.380 --> 00:40:26.769
Who are you?

00:40:26.769 --> 00:40:28.769
I thought you might like a visitor.

00:40:28.769 --> 00:40:29.769
Wilson.

00:40:29.769 --> 00:40:32.769
How do you know me?

00:40:32.769 --> 00:40:33.769
I was in that first.

00:40:33.769 --> 00:40:38.769
facility with you, I know all about your ability to read people like Braille.

00:40:38.769 --> 00:40:40.769
Now tell me.

00:40:40.769 --> 00:40:46.769
That man who stopped you the other night, how much of his story did you get through?

00:40:46.769 --> 00:40:49.769
Let's just say he shouldn't have touched me.

00:40:49.769 --> 00:40:54.150
Guys like him belong in places like Black Creek.

00:40:54.150 --> 00:40:59.760
Why were you in there?

00:40:59.760 --> 00:41:03.269
You don't seem so special.

00:41:03.269 --> 00:41:11.329
The human mind is simply a highly sophisticated computer.

00:41:11.329 --> 00:41:13.329
Download too much information and it crashed.

00:41:13.329 --> 00:41:15.329
and it crashes.

00:41:15.329 --> 00:41:17.329
And all the data's lost.

00:41:17.329 --> 00:41:26.440
Is that supposed to be?

00:41:26.440 --> 00:41:27.440
Let me show you.

